From dcfe616eb171d9fe7db783b721dd55c86460bb1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:10:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 011/144] Input: syna_tcm2: make the Dodge transport and power
 lifecycle robust

Consolidate the local report, SPI transport, modalias, teardown and panel-sleep follow-ups.

Consolidated from local follow-ups:
  70e8fb990dc5d588782863d8f87e21dca5a20213 Input: syna_tcm2: bound reports and balance device resources
  0ad078e0e4d607e8cbf1f789f57e45591c60c9cb Input: syna_tcm2: depend on its SPI transport
  0bd057112672d9398572d707cede76ea4b4cad33 Input: syna_tcm2: export the OF-created SPI modalias
  57ddd9d60ca58565a4974946c8da3b0233645c6a input: syna_tcm2: retain ownership of the static SPI interface
  a496b606f10af2557e5a58c7ac41fdafabfb53ea input: syna_tcm2: detach the borrowed interface on transport removal
  894f8990d3fa52cc6542e1bd89d76619ecc3bab1 input: syna_tcm2: accept an empty uncounted active-object list
  529b4b4076896fd8260a57f7838977c97e8738c7 Input: syna_tcm2 - follow panel sleep without touch wake
